<article class="env-lemma" id="0G80">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G80">Lemma <span data-tag="0G80">37.13.12</span>.</a> Let $X \to Y \to Z$ be morphisms of schemes. Assume $X \to Z$ smooth and $Y \to Z$ étale. Then $X \to Y$ is smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The morphism $X \to Y$ is locally of finite presentation by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FV" data-tag="02FV">29.22.11</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0D0N" data-tag="0D0N">37.13.7</a> we have $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Z}) = 0$ and the module $\Omega _{X/Z}$ is finite locally free. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0G7Z" data-tag="0G7Z">37.13.8</a> we have $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{Y/Z}) = H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{Y/Z}) = 0$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0E44" data-tag="0E44">37.13.10</a> we get $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}) = 0$ and $\Omega _{X/Y} \cong \Omega _{X/Z}$ is finite locally free. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0D0N" data-tag="0D0N">37.13.7</a> the morphism $X \to Y$ is smooth. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>